WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.563
Performance criterion 4.3: escalate each failed action to the appropriate authority.

2
00:00:06.563 --> 00:00:13.606
The Competency Standards list four: the IT department manager, the information security manager,

3
00:00:13.606 --> 00:00:18.962
the security solution vendor, and the chief information security officer.

4
00:00:18.962 --> 00:00:20.943
Our SOP says who gets what.

5
00:00:22.043 --> 00:00:23.601
Here are the rules.

6
00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:28.519
Check them in order, and the first one that matches decides.

7
00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:34.503
E1: ransomware or confirmed data loss on a Tier 1 asset goes to the CISO.

8
00:00:34.503 --> 00:00:42.291
E2: any other failure on a red flag or a Tier 1 asset goes to the information security manager.

9
00:00:42.291 --> 00:00:47.373
E3: if the security product itself failed, open a vendor case.

10
00:00:47.373 --> 00:00:51.636
E4: anything else goes to the IT department manager.

11
00:00:52.735 --> 00:00:54.316
REG-PC-01 first.

12
00:00:54.316 --> 00:01:00.441
It is not ransomware and no data loss is confirmed, so not E1.

13
00:01:00.441 --> 00:01:06.863
But REG-PC-01 is the registrar's PC with student records: Tier 1.

14
00:01:06.863 --> 00:01:11.408
Rule E2 matches: information security manager.

15
00:01:12.508 --> 00:01:13.787
Now MKT-PC-04.

16
00:01:13.787 --> 00:01:18.720
An engine error sounds like a vendor problem, rule E3.

17
00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.730
But we check in order.

18
00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:26.668
Remember Day 5: MKT-PC-04 had a file-infecting virus, a red flag.

19
00:01:26.668 --> 00:01:32.241
So rule E2 matches first: information security manager again.

20
00:01:32.241 --> 00:01:40.372
The vendor can be copied, but the person who decides is the information security manager.

21
00:01:41.472 --> 00:01:45.722
Phone first, then the escalation record by email.

22
00:01:45.722 --> 00:01:47.544
This is the template.

23
00:01:48.644 --> 00:01:51.108
Here is my record for REG-PC-01.

24
00:01:51.108 --> 00:01:57.732
The most important lines: the impact, what is still at risk, and what I need from her.

25
00:01:57.732 --> 00:02:05.280
The target for the information security manager is thirty minutes, so if I called at twelve forty,

26
00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.051
I follow up at one ten.

27
00:02:08.151 --> 00:02:09.051
Your turn.

28
00:02:09.051 --> 00:02:12.380
In the CTM Virtual Lab, choose Day 9.

29
00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:21.198
In Activity 9.3, escalate the six failed actions from the bank and write the record for FIN-PC-03.

30
00:02:21.198 --> 00:02:25.337
Check the tiers and the Day 5 red flags first.

31
00:02:25.337 --> 00:02:31.095
Then in Activity 9.4, follow up your own workstation's scan log.

